[
  {
    "_comment": "SCHEMA EVOLUTION, ClickHouseDest (GENERATED by gen_suites.py; do not edit): the schema_evolution policy end to end, the cases of tabsdata-os' shared schema policy itests -- created_exact, strict_new_column, update_new_column, strict_missing_column, update_missing_column, strict_wider_type, strict_fitting_type, update_wider_type. Every case owns a table (evo_<case>) and is written in two phases from the dev publishers of functions/evo_frames.py: phase 1 seeds every table, phase 2 writes the frame under test (the writes that must succeed first, then the ones that may fail, triggered by verify_evo.py --trigger, which accepts tdk's failed exit and judges by the workers), each publisher a non-detached trigger; after each phase scripts/verify_evo.py reads every table from clickhouse itself and fails unless it holds exactly the plan's state, and after phase 2 also unless every refused write's worker log carries the refusal (SQL_COMMON_10). No monitor stage: refused writes fail their transactions on purpose. Run: `tdd xp one-shot --suite schema-evolution/clickhouse`."
  },
